  "semantics": "Per-file line budget for the production files that exceed the threshold, owned by src/test-kernel/architecture/fileSizeRatchet.vitest.ts (.agents/docs/proposed/process/2026-09-20-agent-refactorability-gates.md section 4). Scope: *.ts, *.tsx, *.mts and *.cts under src/ and packages/*/src/, excluding src/test-kernel/ and *.d.ts. A line is a newline-terminated line, wc -l semantics. Shrink-only in both directions of the edit: a listed file whose line count GREW fails, and a file above the threshold that is absent from `files` fails, so no new oversized file can land. A listed file that shrank does NOT fail (unlike the effect-migration ratchet, whose counts must match exactly): the budget exists to stop growth, and re-pinning every listed file on every deleted line would make the ratchet the reason nobody deletes lines. Headroom is reclaimed by the two staleness rules the suite does enforce: a listed file that no longer exists, and a listed file that has fallen to or below the threshold, both fail until the entry is removed. Lower an entry whenever a PR cuts a file materially, and never raise one: the suite compares files against these numbers and cannot see that a number itself went up, so that half is an author rule enforced in review.",
